    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule with minimal structural impact by adding it as a new, self-contained unit rather than modifying any existing method:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `setBulkSignupWarning(...)`.\n\n2. **`OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a small `@ControllerAdvice` `ResponseBodyAdvice` that, on any outgoing `OwnerDto`, counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's effective business day and sets the flag to `true` when that count exceeds 80, else `false`. It reuses the existing package-private `RegistrationBusinessDay` helper, matching the codebase's \"one small advice per rule\" pattern.\n\nThis keeps every changed function trivial (the two new methods have CC 1\u20132 with essentially no surrounding class complexity) and avoids touching the controller, service, model, or mapper. It applies uniformly to `GET`, `POST`, and other single-owner responses \u2014 the acceptance test's fresh-create case correctly reads `false`.",
